# route: level=w3_l1_coop difficulty=expert players=2 ends=exit after=level:w3_l1b_coop expect=wipes:0,eggs:0,x2_gates:2,min_checkpoints:3
# w3_l1_coop Expert two-stream route: "Frost Summit" for two (designer DB2; ticks:P1|P2, keys L R U D F K S; recorded
# from closed-loop duo bots, build/db2/bot_w3_l1_coop.gd). As the Beginner route: the ramp-top Shellback pincer, the
# floes, gate 'lake' (both crouch side by side in the ice tunnel: the Brace Wall stops the Bull Rex, they club it while
# it is dazed and the ice door opens), the ledge zigzag, gate 'cliff' (P1 hops off P2's head onto the clifftop and
# clubs the coiled vine down), the valley pincer; at the water pit both wait facing the slope until the ridge chargers
# have rushed down into the pit, keep clear of its icy lip, then the slope-top pincer (P2 baits from the half slope,
# P1 clubs its back) and up the ridge and the summit steps through the Expert hoppers into the exit.
# Re-recorded by enemies-A (wf10) for the heavy-keeper ruling of G3 with the same bot: the Bull Rex is hurt only
# while the Brace Wall staggers it, one hit per strike (hp 100: five strikes of the pair in one daze); before, the
# pair's club boxes hit it on every tick of a swing.
# Re-recorded in wf11 (levels) with the same closed-loop bot for the gate rules of the round (DESIGN G71-G76:
# in a tablet's ward no enemy gives lift, rest or a pogo; a spring is a launch; an idle hero holds no view).
